  "transcript": "Question\nWhat does the bike workshop guarantee cover, and do I need my ticket?\n\nTool call\ncited_ask {\"question\":\"What does the bike workshop guarantee cover, and do I need my ticket?\"}\n\nTool result\nThe guarantee covers the work on every repair for 90 days, while parts carry the guarantee of their maker [1]. You do not strictly need the ticket: you are asked to bring it, but without it the repair can still be looked up by the frame number [1].\n\nSources:\n1. bike-workshop-policies.md · Guarantee (position 4)\nGuarantee Every repair carries a 90 day guarantee on the work. Parts carry the guarantee of their maker. Bring the ticket; without it we can still look up the repair by the frame number.\n\nAnswer\n**The guarantee:** Every repair carries a **90-day guarantee on the work**. Parts are covered by **the guarantee of their maker** (i.e., the manufacturer's warranty, not the workshop's own) [1].\n\n**The ticket:** You're asked to bring it, but it isn't strictly required — without it, the workshop can still look up your repair **by the frame number** [1].\n\nSource:\n1. bike-workshop-policies.md · Guarantee",
